<main id="main" class="wrap interior"><p class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</p><h1>A little more space.<br><em>A little less pressure.</em></h1><p class="intro">Mental Health Matters began with a simple idea: make it easier to pause, understand yourself, and find somewhere to turn.</p><section class="content-panel" id="understand"><p class="eyebrow">UNDERSTAND</p><h2>Mental health is part of everyday life.</h2><p>Our mental well-being shapes how we experience life, connect with others, and handle challenges. It is influenced by our circumstances and surroundings, as well as our individual experiences.</p><p>There isn’t one way to feel, or one path forward. This site offers a small space for reflection and links to further support.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/mental-health-strengthening-our-response">Read more about mental health at WHO ↗</a></section><div class="two-column"><section class="content-panel green-card"><h2>Made for small moments.</h2><p>Check in with how you feel. Take a quiet minute. Reach out when you want company. You can start anywhere.</p><a class="text-link" href="/#check-in">Try a check-in →</a></section><section class="content-panel lavender"><h2>Your space stays yours.</h2><p>Your check-in is never saved or sent to a server. Only your light or dark theme preference is stored in this browser.</p><p>This is an awareness project, not a clinical service or a substitute for professional care.</p></section></div></main>
